speechtext:
The payments are set out in the Auditor General's Report by

provinces as follows:	Ontario, $24,048.58;
Quebec, $34,382.67; New Brunswick, $8,812.40; Nova Scotia, $5,320.55; Manitoba, $5,205; British Columbia, $13,295; making a total, with the amounts expended in Prince Edward Island, Alberta, Saskatchewan and the Yukon, of $94,346.
